                                        "entry_id": "c5fe2602-6950-39be-8eee-e6c47685dc6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extreme manifestation of a pyrocumulus, generated by the heat of a wildfire, that often rises to the upper troposphere or lower stratosphere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6464bea-0468-46bb-a7f8-1b1812a65c55",
                                                "sense_id": "14e065ae-7a71-3ed9-b6c3-582ca5261809",
                                                "text": "An analysis of how this tornado formed sees several factors joining forces: the preexisting winds and local topography, a pyrocumulonimbus storm developing, and the addition of hotter-burning fuels as the fire hit groups of houses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fe67b0c-784b-46c3-962b-2d51d498a486",
                                                "sense_id": "14e065ae-7a71-3ed9-b6c3-582ca5261809",
                                                "text": "Last Wednesday, though, conditions led to the creation of a larger, taller cloud called a pyrocumulonimbus, which is similar to a thunderhead. It likely reached an altitude of about 45,000 feet, said Neil Lareau, who studies wildfire behavior at the University of Nevada, Reno."
                                            }
                                        ]
